WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:01.860
- [Narrator] In late October,

00:00:01.860 --> 00:00:04.020
workers in China lined up for quarantine.

00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:06.720
Then others rushed to leave
their jobs and some clashed

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:08.664
with police in COVID protective suits.

00:00:08.664 --> 00:00:10.470
(crowd shouting)

00:00:10.470 --> 00:00:13.740
These are images of the chaos
that erupted at a Foxconn site

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:14.688
in Zhengzhou, China

00:00:14.688 --> 00:00:17.433
where the majority of
Apple's iPhones are made.

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:20.850
Now holiday shoppers this
Christmas season are stuck

00:00:20.850 --> 00:00:22.170
with long wait times,

00:00:22.170 --> 00:00:24.180
and Apple warned its Pro model shipments

00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:26.389
would be lower than expected.

00:00:26.389 --> 00:00:27.450
(protestor speaking in foreign language)

00:00:27.450 --> 00:00:29.700
- [Narrator] So here's what
led to the protest at Foxconn

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:31.593
and what that means for your iPhone.

00:00:32.901 --> 00:00:34.590
(camera snapping)

00:00:34.590 --> 00:00:36.180
In late September, the travel season

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:38.910
for China's week-long
National Day holiday began

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:40.890
and people hit the road.

00:00:40.890 --> 00:00:43.200
When residents returned from
other parts of the country,

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:45.930
that's when COVID-19 broke out Zhengzhou.

00:00:45.930 --> 00:00:47.190
The virus eventually spread

00:00:47.190 --> 00:00:49.256
to Foxconn's vast manufacturing site

00:00:49.256 --> 00:00:52.123
where the company enforced
strict COVID controls.

00:00:52.123 --> 00:00:55.350
(worker speaking in foreign language)

00:00:55.350 --> 00:00:57.210
- [Narrator] By late October,
some workers were sent

00:00:57.210 --> 00:00:59.070
to quarantine centers.

00:00:59.070 --> 00:00:59.903
Others were confined

00:00:59.903 --> 00:01:02.070
to unfinished apartment buildings nearby,

00:01:02.070 --> 00:01:04.516
and they were filmed
screaming in frustration.

00:01:04.516 --> 00:01:06.330
(workers shouting)

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:08.400
Meanwhile, some employees
were asked to move out

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:10.740
of their dorms and sleep
in the factory hallways

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:12.243
to keep production running.

00:01:13.770 --> 00:01:15.000
Worried about catching COVID,

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:18.333
on October 29th, thousands
of workers fled the facility.

00:01:19.590 --> 00:01:22.080
Some people boarded buses
after hearing rumors

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:24.420
that infected employees
were being allowed to work

00:01:24.420 --> 00:01:25.803
to meet production goals.

00:01:26.808 --> 00:01:28.500
(clock ticking)

00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:29.550
To replace those who left,

00:01:29.550 --> 00:01:32.940
recruitment ads started
popping up on November 7th.

00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:35.520
These ads promised quarantine
allowances and bonuses

00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:38.223
for people who would
work for 30 or 60 days.

00:01:40.236 --> 00:01:42.450
(protestor speaking in foreign language)

00:01:42.450 --> 00:01:44.610
- [Narrator] But things came
to a head on November 23rd

00:01:44.610 --> 00:01:45.990
when new recruits got angry

00:01:45.990 --> 00:01:48.300
over what they said were
delayed bonus payments

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:49.939
and conditions at the plant.

00:01:49.939 --> 00:01:52.689
(crowd shouting)

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:55.290
To control the outrage,

00:01:55.290 --> 00:01:58.023
police were deployed,
beating and chasing workers.

00:01:59.550 --> 00:02:02.280
The next day, many employees
lined up at a train station

00:02:02.280 --> 00:02:06.270
after taking up Foxconn's
offer of $1,400 to leave.

00:02:06.270 --> 00:02:08.340
The company also said it
would guarantee recruits

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:10.440
would be paid in line with official ads

00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:11.700
and blamed a computer error

00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:13.233
for some of the pay issues.

00:02:14.430 --> 00:02:16.110
The staff shortage has added pressure

00:02:16.110 --> 00:02:18.300
to the tech giant's iPhone production

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:21.270
as Foxconn Zhengzhou facility makes 85%

00:02:21.270 --> 00:02:23.880
of the Pro line up of iPhones.

00:02:23.880 --> 00:02:25.920
This means customers who
ordered their smartphones

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:29.703
in October or November may not
even get it before Christmas.

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:32.880
To see why, take a look at this graph.

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:36.000
When Apple launched the
iPhone 14 Pro in September,

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:39.120
the wait time was 32 days
during the first week.

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:41.100
Then it started to decrease.

00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:43.140
This is pretty typical
when there's a new launch

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:45.300
like with the iPhone 13 Pro.

00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:48.000
But when COVID hit the
Zhengzhou plant in October,

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:50.850
the wait time went up and
eventually hit 37 days

00:02:50.850 --> 00:02:53.070
by late November, which is the longest

00:02:53.070 --> 00:02:55.530
in the product's 15-year history.

00:02:55.530 --> 00:02:57.060
Apple didn't respond to a request

00:02:57.060 --> 00:02:59.103
for comment about the iPhone delays.

00:03:00.420 --> 00:03:01.920
Meanwhile, steps are being taken

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:04.680
to mitigate the ripple
effects of the disruptions.

00:03:04.680 --> 00:03:07.650
Foxconn has tried to
increase iPhone 14 production

00:03:07.650 --> 00:03:09.420
at other sites in the country,

00:03:09.420 --> 00:03:11.820
according to people
familiar with the matter.

00:03:11.820 --> 00:03:13.290
China's rigid COVID controls,

00:03:13.290 --> 00:03:15.990
among other issues have
also prompted Apple to look

00:03:15.990 --> 00:03:20.100
beyond the mainland, particularly
in India and Vietnam.

00:03:20.100 --> 00:03:22.770
And this could mean in the
future many of our iPhones

00:03:22.770 --> 00:03:26.073
start coming not from China
but from other countries.

